From 3fba20e1f407e7d357b50a02e248e19f5053e781 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:17:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): face unlock lockout settings of snaptop-linux's
 s15-face

snaptop-linux (a SteamOS install on the ASUS Vivobook S 15) runs
Biopass's helper through its own gate, s15-face, which counts false
faces like wrong PINs: a run ends after some, face waits after more and
turns off until a password login. Those numbers are root's
(/etc/s15-face.conf): any program running as the user can write
config.yaml.

A card shows them (`s15-face lockout keys` and `s15-face lockout`) with
the user's count (`s15-face status <user>`), and changes them in one go
through `pkexec /usr/lib/s15-face/s15-face-lockout set KEY VALUE ...` or
`reset-defaults` (its own polkit action, administrator password, shipped
by snaptop-linux, not here). Without /usr/local/sbin/s15-face the card
is not shown. Not for upstream: it names snaptop-linux's paths.
Tests: lockout (parsing, arguments, exit codes, reading through a stub
tool), lockoutInputs.test.ts.
